Dataset and Document Collection Summary

Overview
As part of the data collection phase, sample business datasets and workforce documents were gathered
and prepared to support the development of the AI-Powered Business Verification and Workforce
Automation System. These resources will be used for database population, business verification
testing, document processing, OCR evaluation, information extraction, and workflow automation.

Business Dataset Collection
A sample dataset containing 50 business records was created to simulate real-world business
verification scenarios. The dataset includes organizations from multiple industries such as
technology, healthcare, logistics, finance, retail, manufacturing, marketing, consulting, and human
resources.

Available Data Fields
- Business Name
- Website
- Phone Number
- Email Address
- Industry
- Business Status (Active, Pending, Inactive)

Purpose
The business dataset will support:
- Business verification testing
- Entity matching and record validation
- Database development and integration
- AI-powered confidence scoring and discrepancy detection

Workforce Document Collection
A collection of sample workforce and business-related documents was assembled to support document
processing and automation workflows.

Document Types Collected
- Employee Onboarding Forms
- Employment Verification Letters
- Business Licenses
- Compliance Certificates
- Vendor Registration Forms
- W-9 Forms
- Insurance Certificates
- Invoices
- Employee Training Records
- Background Check Reports

Purpose
These documents will be used to:
- Test OCR and text extraction functionality
- Validate information extraction models
- Simulate business verification workflows
- Support workforce automation processes
- Evaluate document classification capabilities

Project Impact
The collected datasets and documents provide the foundation for the project's verification and
automation components. They allow the development team to begin implementing database operations,
document ingestion, information extraction, and workflow automation features without relying on
sensitive or proprietary business records.

Current Status
- 50 Sample Business Records Prepared
- Multiple Workforce Document Types Collected
- Data Ready for Database Integration
- Resources Available for AI and OCR Testing

Next Steps
- Load business records into the project database
- Connect document storage to the processing pipeline
- Begin OCR and information extraction testing
- Integrate verification workflows with backend services
